From: gt510 <gt510@localhost>
Subject: media: qcom: camss: restore the MSM8916 VFE PIX line

Since 7c1340e4c296 ("media: qcom: camss: Assign the correct number of RDIs
per VFE") vfe_res_8x16 has line_num = 3, meant as "3 RDIs". But the VFE
code creates lines 0..line_num-1 and VFE_LINE_PIX is 3, so the PIX line
(msm_vfe0_pix, the only path that outputs NV12/NV16 from YUV sensors) was
no longer registered on MSM8916; before that commit 8x16 used
VFE_LINE_NUM_GEN1 = 4. Restore 4.

On SM-T550 the front SR200PC20 (UYVY) then can deliver NV12, which the
Adreno 306 imports into GL; UYVY dmabufs fail EGLImage import (0x3003) and
GTK falls back to an mmap download + upload per frame.
---
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss.c
@@ -150,7 +150,12 @@
 		.reg = { "vfe0" },
 		.interrupt = { "vfe0" },
 		.vfe = {
-			.line_num = 3,
+			/*
+			 * 3 RDIs + the PIX line (VFE_LINE_PIX = 3): the VFE
+			 * code creates lines 0..line_num-1, so 3 dropped PIX
+			 * (and its NV12/NV16 output) on MSM8916.
+			 */
+			.line_num = 4,
 			.hw_ops = &vfe_ops_4_1,
 			.formats_rdi = &vfe_formats_rdi_8x16,
 			.formats_pix = &vfe_formats_pix_8x16
